<div class="chr-content-container">
<div class="content orcanex-refund-policy">
<h1>Refund Policy</h1>
<p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> 15 September 2026
                                    At <strong>Orcanex</strong> (“Orcanex”, “we”, “us” or “our”), we aim to provide
                                    professional digital, website, marketing and related services to a high standard.
                                    This Refund Policy explains when refunds may or may not be available.
                                    This policy must be read together with any proposal, quotation, service agreement,
                                    scope of work or other terms agreed between Orcanex and the client.
                                    Nothing in this Refund Policy is intended to exclude, restrict or modify any rights
                                    or remedies that cannot lawfully be excluded under the <strong>Australian Consumer
                                        Law (ACL)</strong> or other applicable Australian law.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>1. Australian Consumer Law</h2>
<p>Our services come with consumer guarantees that cannot be excluded where the
                                    Australian Consumer Law applies.
                                    Depending on the circumstances, these guarantees may include that services will:</p>
<ul>
<li>Be provided with due care and skill;</li>
<li>Be reasonably fit for a purpose made known to us;</li>
<li>Achieve a particular result where that result has been made known and relied
                                        upon, where applicable; and</li>
<li>Be supplied within a reasonable time where no specific timeframe has been
                                        agreed.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where a service does not meet an applicable consumer guarantee, you may be entitled
                                    to a remedy under the Australian Consumer Law.
                                    Nothing in this policy limits those statutory rights.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>2. General Refund Policy</h2>
<p>Except where required by applicable law, refund requests are assessed on a
                                    case-by-case basis having regard to:</p>
<ul>
<li>The services purchased;</li>
<li>The work already performed;</li>
<li>The stage of the project;</li>
<li>Third-party costs already incurred;</li>
<li>Client approvals;</li>
<li>The agreed scope of work;</li>
<li>The circumstances giving rise to the request; and</li>
<li>Any applicable consumer law obligations.</li>
</ul>
<p>Submitting a refund request does not automatically entitle a client to a refund.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>3. Change-of-Mind Refunds</h2>
<p>Unless otherwise expressly agreed in writing, Orcanex does not provide refunds merely
                                    because a client:</p>
<ul>
<li>Changes their mind;</li>
<li>Changes business direction;</li>
<li>No longer requires the service;</li>
<li>Experiences changes in personal or financial circumstances;</li>
<li>Disagrees with a business partner;</li>
<li>Decides to use another provider;</li>
<li>Cancels a project for convenience; or</li>
<li>No longer wishes to proceed for reasons unrelated to a failure by Orcanex to
                                        provide the agreed service.</li>
</ul>
<p>This does not affect any rights the client may have under applicable law.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>4. Work Already Performed</h2>
<p>Where a project has commenced, amounts relating to work already properly performed
                                    are generally non-refundable, except where otherwise required by law.
                                    This may include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Research;</li>
<li>Strategy;</li>
<li>Planning;</li>
<li>Consultation;</li>
<li>Wireframes;</li>
<li>Design concepts;</li>
<li>Website development;</li>
<li>Coding;</li>
<li>Content preparation;</li>
<li>Creative production;</li>
<li>Campaign setup;</li>
<li>Technical configuration;</li>
<li>Revisions;</li>
<li>Meetings; and</li>
<li>Project management.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where a refund is legally required or otherwise approved, Orcanex may take into
                                    account the reasonable value of services already provided, to the extent permitted
                                    by law.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>5. Client Approval of Work</h2>
<p>Except where applicable law provides otherwise, a refund will generally not be
                                    available for a deliverable or project stage that the client has reviewed and
                                    expressly approved.
                                    Examples may include approval of:</p>
<ul>
<li>Website designs;</li>
<li>Mock-ups;</li>
<li>Demo links;</li>
<li>Prototypes;</li>
<li>Wireframes;</li>
<li>Logos;</li>
<li>Graphics;</li>
<li>Written content;</li>
<li>Advertising creatives;</li>
<li>Development milestones; or</li>
<li>Other agreed deliverables.</li>
</ul>
<p>Approval may be provided in writing, including through email, messaging platforms,
                                    project-management systems or other agreed communication channels.
                                    Approval does not remove any rights that cannot lawfully be excluded under
                                    Australian law.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>6. Revisions and Scope Changes</h2>
<p>Refunds will generally not be provided because a client requests work beyond the
                                    agreed scope.
                                    Additional work may include:</p>
<ul>
<li>New pages;</li>
<li>Additional design concepts;</li>
<li>New functionality;</li>
<li>New integrations;</li>
<li>Additional revisions;</li>
<li>Changed requirements;</li>
<li>New content;</li>
<li>Additional campaigns; or</li>
<li>Work not included in the original quotation or scope.</li>
</ul>
<p>Additional work may be quoted and charged separately.
                                    Where a package includes a specified number of design concepts or revision rounds,
                                    additional concepts or revisions may incur additional charges.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>7. Third-Party Products and Services</h2>
<p>Fees paid or committed to third-party providers may be non-refundable where those
                                    third parties do not provide Orcanex with a refund.
                                    These costs may include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Domain registrations;</li>
<li>Domain renewals;</li>
<li>Website hosting;</li>
<li>Email hosting;</li>
<li>SSL certificates;</li>
<li>Software licences;</li>
<li>Plugins;</li>
<li>Themes;</li>
<li>Stock photography;</li>
<li>Premium fonts;</li>
<li>SaaS subscriptions;</li>
<li>Advertising spend;</li>
<li>Third-party API fees;</li>
<li>Platform fees; and</li>
<li>Other third-party products or services.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where a third-party refund is available, Orcanex may pass on the relevant refundable
                                    amount to the client after deducting any legitimate non-refundable costs, fees or
                                    work already performed, where permitted by law.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>8. Digital Marketing Services</h2>
<p>Services involving ongoing labour, campaign management or third-party advertising
                                    expenditure are generally not refundable for periods in which the service has
                                    already been properly provided.
                                    These services may include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Search Engine Optimisation (SEO);</li>
<li>Google Ads management;</li>
<li>Microsoft Advertising;</li>
<li>Meta advertising;</li>
<li>Social Media Management;</li>
<li>Social Media Optimisation;</li>
<li>Content marketing;</li>
<li>Copywriting;</li>
<li>Campaign management;</li>
<li>Analytics and reporting;</li>
<li>Website maintenance;</li>
<li>Hosting management; and</li>
<li>Other ongoing marketing or technical services.</li>
</ul>
<p>Advertising spend paid directly or indirectly to third-party platforms is subject to
                                    the relevant platform’s own terms and refund policies.
                                    Nothing in this section affects any remedy that may be available under applicable
                                    Australian law.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>9. Website and Design Projects</h2>
<p>Once a website, design or other deliverable has been completed and accepted by the
                                    client, amounts paid are generally non-refundable except where required by law.
                                    A client will also generally not be entitled to a refund merely because they request
                                    stylistic changes after having previously approved the relevant design direction or
                                    deliverable.
                                    Any additional work requested after approval may be treated as a variation to scope.
                                </p>
<hr/>
<h2>10. Project Timelines</h2>
<p>Any project delivery timeframe stated by Orcanex is an estimate unless expressly
                                    agreed in writing as a fixed deadline.
                                    Typical estimated delivery periods may include:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Logo Design Projects:</strong> approximately 1–2 business days;</li>
<li><strong>Website Design Projects:</strong> approximately 5–7 business days;</li>
<li><strong>Custom Development Projects:</strong> as specified in the relevant
                                        proposal or project scope.</li>
</ul>
<p>Timeframes may be affected by:</p>
<ul>
<li>Project complexity;</li>
<li>Client responsiveness;</li>
<li>Delays in receiving information or content;</li>
<li>Revision requests;</li>
<li>Scope changes;</li>
<li>Third-party providers;</li>
<li>Technical requirements;</li>
<li>Public holidays;</li>
<li>Platform outages;</li>
<li>Force majeure events; and</li>
<li>Other matters reasonably outside Orcanex’s control.</li>
</ul>
<p>A reasonable delay alone will not automatically entitle a client to a refund.
                                    However, nothing in this section limits rights that may arise where services are not
                                    supplied within the period required under applicable law or an expressly agreed
                                    contractual term.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>11. Client Delays and Project Inactivity</h2>
<p>Clients are responsible for providing required feedback, information, content, access
                                    credentials and approvals within a reasonable timeframe.
                                    If a client does not respond for <strong>10 calendar days</strong>, Orcanex may
                                    place the project on hold.
                                    We may contact the client before closing or archiving an inactive project.
                                    If the client remains unresponsive for a prolonged period, Orcanex may consider the
                                    active project phase suspended or administratively closed.
                                    Any restart may be subject to:</p>
<ul>
<li>Availability;</li>
<li>A revised project schedule;</li>
<li>Reconfirmation of requirements; and</li>
<li>Additional reasonable fees where substantial rework or remobilisation is
                                        required.</li>
</ul>
<p>Amounts relating to work already performed remain payable, subject to any rights
                                    available under applicable law.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>12. Cancellation by the Client</h2>
<p>A client may request cancellation of a project by contacting Orcanex.
                                    Where cancellation occurs after work has commenced, the client may remain
                                    responsible for:</p>
<ul>
<li>Work already completed;</li>
<li>Work reasonably undertaken prior to cancellation;</li>
<li>Third-party costs already incurred or committed;</li>
<li>Non-refundable external fees; and</li>
<li>Any other amounts properly payable under the agreed service arrangement.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where the client has paid more than the amount properly chargeable for work completed
                                    and non-refundable costs, any remaining amount may be refundable where appropriate.
                                </p>
<hr/>
<h2>13. Refund Requests</h2>
<p>Refund requests should be submitted as soon as reasonably practicable after the issue
                                    arises.
                                    Requests should include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Client name;</li>
<li>Project or invoice details;</li>
<li>The service purchased;</li>
<li>The reason for the request; and</li>
<li>Relevant supporting information.</li>
</ul>
<p>Refund requests may be sent to:
                                    <strong>info@orcanex.com.au</strong>
                                    We will assess requests reasonably and in accordance with applicable Australian law.
                                    A contractual or administrative time period for submitting refund requests does not
                                    override any rights or remedies that cannot lawfully be limited under the Australian
                                    Consumer Law.
                                </p>
<hr/>
<h2>14. Problems With Services</h2>
<p>If you believe there is a problem with a service provided by Orcanex, please contact
                                    us as soon as reasonably possible.
                                    Where appropriate, Orcanex may first be entitled or required to assess the issue
                                    and, depending on the circumstances, may offer to:</p>
<ul>
<li>Correct the issue;</li>
<li>Re-perform affected work;</li>
<li>Complete outstanding work;</li>
<li>Provide another appropriate remedy; or</li>
<li>Provide a refund or partial refund where required or otherwise appropriate.</li>
</ul>
<p>The appropriate remedy will depend on the circumstances and applicable Australian
                                    law.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>15. Website Security and Third-Party Issues</h2>
<p>Following website handover or launch, Orcanex is not generally responsible for issues
                                    caused solely by circumstances outside our reasonable control, including:</p>
<ul>
<li>Client modifications;</li>
<li>Third-party plugins;</li>
<li>Third-party themes;</li>
<li>External hosting providers;</li>
<li>Malware introduced after handover;</li>
<li>Hacking or unauthorised access not caused by our failure;</li>
<li>Unsupported software;</li>
<li>Failure to install updates;</li>
<li>Third-party API changes;</li>
<li>Platform changes; or</li>
<li>The client’s failure to maintain appropriate security measures.</li>
</ul>
<p>This does not exclude responsibility where a problem is caused by Orcanex’s failure
                                    to exercise a standard of care required by applicable law.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>16. Maintenance Services</h2>
<p>Unless a maintenance service is included in the agreed scope, completion of a website
                                    project does not automatically include indefinite:</p>
<ul>
<li>Website maintenance;</li>
<li>Security monitoring;</li>
<li>Updates;</li>
<li>Backups;</li>
<li>Content changes;</li>
<li>Plugin maintenance;</li>
<li>Technical support; or</li>
<li>Malware removal.</li>
</ul>
<p>The absence of a maintenance plan does not itself remove any legal rights relating to
                                    the original services provided.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>17. Intellectual Property Following a Refund</h2>
<p>Where Orcanex provides a full refund for a deliverable and the refund results in
                                    termination of the client’s entitlement to that deliverable, intellectual property
                                    rights in unpaid or refunded work will remain with Orcanex to the extent permitted
                                    by law and subject to any separate written agreement.
                                    Unless otherwise agreed, the client must not continue to use a fully refunded
                                    deliverable where ownership or usage rights were conditional upon payment.
                                    Where only a partial refund is provided, intellectual property ownership and licence
                                    rights will be determined by:</p>
<ul>
<li>The applicable service agreement;</li>
<li>The portion of work paid for;</li>
<li>Any written settlement; and</li>
<li>Applicable law.</li>
</ul>
<hr/>
<h2>18. Chargebacks and Payment Disputes</h2>
<p>Clients are encouraged to contact Orcanex before initiating a payment dispute or
                                    chargeback so that we have an opportunity to review and resolve the issue.
                                    Nothing in this section prevents a client from exercising any lawful rights
                                    available through their payment provider or applicable law.
                                    Submitting false or misleading information in connection with a payment dispute may
                                    result in Orcanex providing relevant project, transaction and communication records
                                    to the applicable financial institution or payment provider.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>19. Right to Refuse, Suspend or Terminate Services</h2>
<p>Orcanex may refuse, suspend or terminate services where reasonably necessary,
                                    including where:</p>
<ul>
<li>Required by law;</li>
<li>A client fails to pay amounts properly due;</li>
<li>A client materially breaches an agreement;</li>
<li>A client engages in abusive, threatening, fraudulent or unlawful conduct;</li>
<li>Continuing the service creates a material security risk;</li>
<li>A client requests unlawful activity; or</li>
<li>Continuing the project is no longer reasonably practicable.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where Orcanex terminates a service, fees and any refund entitlement will be
                                    determined having regard to work already completed, third-party costs, the reason
                                    for termination, the applicable agreement and Australian law.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>20. No Guarantee of Marketing Results</h2>
<p>Marketing, advertising and SEO services involve factors outside Orcanex’s control.
                                    Unless expressly agreed in writing, we do not guarantee:</p>
<ul>
<li>Specific Google rankings;</li>
<li>A particular number of leads;</li>
<li>Specific sales volumes;</li>
<li>Particular advertising costs;</li>
<li>Revenue increases;</li>
<li>Social media growth;</li>
<li>Conversion rates; or</li>
<li>Other specific commercial outcomes.</li>
</ul>
<p>We will provide agreed services with the level of care and skill required by
                                    applicable law.
                                    A campaign failing to achieve a client’s desired commercial result does not by
                                    itself mean the service was defective or create an automatic entitlement to a
                                    refund.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>21. Relationship With Other Agreements</h2>
<p>This Refund Policy should be read together with:</p>
<ul>
<li>Any quotation;</li>
<li>Proposal;</li>
<li>Scope of work;</li>
<li>Service agreement;</li>
<li>Terms and Conditions; and</li>
<li>Other written agreement between Orcanex and the client.</li>
</ul>
<p>If there is an inconsistency, the specific written agreement relating to the relevant
                                    service may apply to the extent permitted by law.
                                    Nothing in any agreement excludes rights that cannot legally be excluded.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>22. Changes to This Refund Policy</h2>
<p>We may update this Refund Policy from time to time.
                                    The current version will be published on our website with an updated revision date.
                                    Changes will not retrospectively remove statutory rights or contractual rights
                                    already accrued.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>23. Contact Us</h2>
<p>For questions about this Refund Policy or to submit a refund request, please contact:
                                    <strong>Orcanex</strong>
<strong>Email:</strong> info@orcanex.com.au
                                    <strong>Phone:</strong> +61 480 009 553
                                    <strong>Address:</strong> Level 3, 530 Lt Collins Street, Melbourne VIC, Australia
                                    <strong>Website:</strong> orcanex.com.au
                                    <strong>Effective Date:</strong> 23 June 2026
                                    <strong>Last Updated:</strong> 15 September 2026
                                </p>
</div>
</div>
